# Runtime outputs
*.log
# Corpus directories, anchored to where projects actually keep them.
#
# This was a bare `data` line, which matches a directory of that name at ANY depth —
# so it silently excluded every project's `src/gpt/data/` SOURCE package too. The
# result: none of the from_scratch projects had their data package in git at all, and
# a fresh clone produced a tree where `trainer.py`'s `from ..data import ...` fails.
# Re-including files under an excluded directory is not possible in git (it never
# descends into it), so the pattern has to be anchored rather than negated.
# No trailing slash: these are a real directory in some projects and a symlink to a
# shared corpus in others, and a trailing slash would only match the directory form.
from_scratch/*/data
# Curated QA prompt suites are hand-written test fixtures, not downloaded corpora.
!from_scratch/custom-gpt-153m/data/
!from_scratch/custom-gpt-153m/data/prompt_sets/
!from_scratch/custom-gpt-153m/data/prompt_sets/*.jsonl
from_scratch/_shared_data
fine_tuning/*/data
base_models/*/data
# custom-gpt-nano's data/ is a hand-written, ~5KB bundled corpus that IS meant to be
# committed (the whole point of that project is "no download needed") — unlike every
# other project's data/ (downloaded/generated, intentionally excluded just above).
# Un-ignore the directory itself, then the one file inside it — negating just the file
# doesn't work while git still treats the parent directory as excluded.
!from_scratch/custom-gpt-nano/data
!from_scratch/custom-gpt-nano/data/corpus.txt
# Token files built by `gpt-tokenize`, wherever they land.
*.bin
logs
logs/train_eval_history.csv
# matches at any depth, so this covers every fine-tuning project's outputs/ dir
# (e.g. fine_tuning/tinyllama-1.1b-lora/outputs/, fine_tuning/*/outputs/), not just one
outputs/
checkpoints_archive/
reports/
